Here is a complete breakdown of everything requested, with exact line numbers:

---

## 1. View Modes

```18:21:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
<div v-if="!isTeacher" class="view-tabs">
  <button type="button" :class="{ active: viewMode === 'week' }" @click="viewMode = 'week'">週課表</button>
  <button type="button" :class="{ active: viewMode === 'teacher' }" @click="viewMode = 'teacher'">老師視角</button>
</div>
```

- `week` — the time-grid calendar (default)
- `teacher` — card-based grouped view, only visible to non-teacher roles
- `viewMode` is a `ref` initialized at line 542: `const viewMode = ref('week');`
- When `isTeacher` is true (role === `'teacher'`), the tab switcher is hidden entirely and only the week view is shown as "我的課表".

---

## 2. Course Block Rendering (Week Grid Template)

```58:84:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
<div v-if="viewMode === 'week'" class="week-view">
  <div class="week-grid">
    <div class="time-col">
      <div class="col-header-blank"></div>
      <div v-for="h in hours" :key="h" class="time-label">{{ String(h).padStart(2, '0') }}:00</div>
    </div>
    <div v-for="(dayName, dayIdx) in dayNames" :key="dayIdx" class="day-col">
      <div class="col-header">{{ dayName }}<br/>({{ getDisplayDateString(dayIdx + 1) }})</div>
      <div v-for="h in hours" :key="h" class="slot"
        :class="{ 'no-click': isTeacher }"
        @click="!isTeacher && onSlotClick(dayIdx + 1, h, getDisplayDateFull(dayIdx + 1))"
      >
        <div
          v-for="(course, cIdx) in getCoursesAt(dayIdx + 1, h)"
          :key="course.id"
          class="course-block"
          :style="getCourseBlockStyle(course, dayIdx + 1, h, cIdx)"
          @click.stop="!isTeacher && onCourseClick(course, getDisplayDateFull(dayIdx + 1))"
        >
          <div class="cb-student">{{ course.student_name }}</div>
          <div class="cb-detail">{{ getSubjectLabel(course.subject) }} · {{ course.teacher_name }}</div>
          <div class="cb-type">{{ classTypeLabel(course.class_type) }}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

- The grid is 7 day columns × N hour rows (hours 8–22, line 557).
- `getCoursesAt(dayOfWeek, hour)` filters `filteredCourses` to all courses whose `start_time` hour matches `h` and whose `day_of_week` (or `days_of_week` array) matches the column.
- `getCourseBlockStyle` (lines 706–732) sets `height` based on `duration_hours * 55 - 4px`. For multiple overlapping courses in the same slot it divides the column width equally (`100% / total` per block), positioned with `left: calc(X% + 2px)` and `width: calc(X% - 4px)`.
- Each block shows: student name (`.cb-student`), subject + teacher (`.cb-detail`), class type (`.cb-type`).

---

## 3. Drag Events

**There are no drag-and-drop events.** No `@dragstart`, `@dragover`, `@drop`, or any HTML5 drag API is used anywhere in the file. Interaction is entirely click-based (`@click` on `.slot` and `.course-block`).

---

## 4. onCourseClick, openRescheduleModal, and the Leave Flow

**`onCourseClick`** (lines 1040–1069):

```1040:1069:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const onCourseClick = (course, fullDateStr) => {
  const baseId = course.is_exception ? course.student_course_id : course.id;
  editingCourseId.value = baseId;
  editingActionDate.value = fullDateStr || '';
  conflictWarning.value = '';
  const start = normalizeTimeTo30(course.start_time || '16:00');
  const baseCourse = courses.value.find(c => c.id === baseId) || course;

  modalForm.value = {
    student_id: baseCourse.student_id || course.student_id,
    subject: baseCourse.subject || course.subject,
    teacher_id: baseCourse.teacher_id || course.teacher_id || '',
    class_type: baseCourse.class_type || course.class_type,
    weeks: baseCourse.weeks || [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    day_of_week: course.day_of_week,
    days_of_week: (baseCourse.days_of_week && baseCourse.days_of_week.length)
      ? [...baseCourse.days_of_week]
      : (course.day_of_week != null ? [course.day_of_week] : [1]),
    start_time: start,
    end_time: computeEndTime(start, course.duration_hours || 2),
    duration_hours: course.duration_hours || 2,
    rate_per_30min: baseCourse.rate_per_30min || 500,
    payment_type: baseCourse.payment_type || 'session',
    remaining_sessions: baseCourse.remaining_sessions || 0,
    first_class_date: baseCourse.first_class_date || '',
    action_date: fullDateStr
  };
  syncRatePer2hFromModel();
  showModal.value = true;
};
```

Key behavior: if the clicked block is an exception (reschedule/extra), it resolves back to the original `student_course_id` as `baseId` so the modal shows the parent course. `action_date` stores the exact calendar date clicked for use by the sub-actions.

**`openRescheduleModal`** (lines 1270–1292):

```1270:1292:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const openRescheduleModal = () => {
  const exactDate = modalForm.value.action_date || new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
  const newStart = normalizeTimeTo30(modalForm.value.start_time);
  const dur = modalForm.value.duration_hours || 2;
  rescheduleForm.value = {
    student_id: modalForm.value.student_id,
    subject: modalForm.value.subject,
    course_id: editingCourseId.value,
    original_day: modalForm.value.day_of_week,
    original_start: modalForm.value.start_time,
    original_end: modalForm.value.end_time,
    original_date: exactDate,
    new_date: exactDate,
    new_day_of_week: modalForm.value.day_of_week,
    new_start: newStart,
    new_end: computeEndTime(newStart, dur),
    teacher_id: modalForm.value.teacher_id,
    class_type: modalForm.value.class_type,
    duration_hours: dur
  };
  showModal.value = false;
  showRescheduleModal.value = true;
};
```

`submitReschedule` (lines 1294–1353) writes **two rows** to the `schedules` table:
1. `status: 'rescheduled'` on `original_date` — marks the old occurrence as cancelled.
2. `status: 'scheduled'` on `new_date` — the new occurrence that will appear in the grid.

**Leave Flow** (`openLeaveModal` → `submitLeave`, lines 1145–1181):

```1145:1181:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const openLeaveModal = () => {
  const exactDate = modalForm.value.action_date || new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
  leaveForm.value = {
    student_id: modalForm.value.student_id,
    subject: modalForm.value.subject,
    day_of_week: modalForm.value.day_of_week,
    start_time: modalForm.value.start_time,
    end_time: modalForm.value.end_time,
    schedule_date: exactDate,
    course_id: editingCourseId.value
  };
  showModal.value = false;
  showLeaveModal.value = true;
};
```

`submitLeave` inserts one row into `schedules` with `status: 'leave'`, `deduction: 0`. This is the exception record that `filteredCourses` checks against to suppress the regular block for that date (line 772–776).

---

## 5. getDisplayDateFull and Week Navigation

```669:686:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const getDisplayDateFull = (dayOfWeek) => {
  const weekNum = displayWeek.value || 1;
  const year = displayYear.value;
  const month = displayMonth.value;
  const refMonday = getMondayOfMonthWeek(year, month, weekNum);
  const actualMonday = addDays(refMonday, weekOffset.value * 7);
  return addDays(actualMonday, dayOfWeek - 1);
};

const prevWeek = () => { weekOffset.value -= 1; };
const nextWeek = () => { weekOffset.value += 1; };

const getDisplayDateString = (dayOfWeek) => {
  const full = getDisplayDateFull(dayOfWeek);
  if (!full) return '';
  const [, m, d] = full.split('-');
  return `${parseInt(m)}/${parseInt(d)}`;
};
```

- `getMondayOfMonthWeek(year, month, weekNum)` (lines 524–532) finds the Monday of the Nth week of a given month (aligns to the ISO Monday-start week containing the 1st of the month).
- `weekOffset` shifts that Monday by ±7 days, so "上週 / 下週" buttons move the view without changing `displayWeek` or `displayMonth`.
- When `displayWeek` changes (watch at line 1362), `weekOffset` resets to 0.
- When `prevMonth` / `nextMonth` is called, both `displayWeek` and `weekOffset` reset to 0 (lines 508–509, 519–520).

---

## 6. filteredCourses Computed Property

```756:820:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const filteredCourses = computed(() => {
  let list = displayWeekFilteredCourses.value;
  if (filterTeacherId.value) {
    list = list.filter(c => c.teacher_id === filterTeacherId.value);
  }

  if (viewMode.value === 'week') {
    const mergedList = [];
    // Pass 1: regular classes — skip if a leave/rescheduled exception exists for this exact date
    list.forEach(c => {
      const days = (c.days_of_week && c.days_of_week.length) ? c.days_of_week : [parseInt(c.day_of_week) || 0];
      days.forEach(dow => {
        const targetDate = getDisplayDateFull(dow);
        if (!targetDate) return;
        const hasException = exceptions.value.some(ex =>
          (ex.status === 'leave' || ex.status === 'rescheduled') &&
          ex.student_course_id === c.id &&
          ex.schedule_date === targetDate
        );
        const isBeforeStart = c.first_class_date && String(targetDate).trim() < String(c.first_class_date).trim();
        if (!hasException && !isBeforeStart) {
          mergedList.push({ ...c, day_of_week: dow, days_of_week: [dow], is_base: true });
        }
      });
    });

    // Pass 2: exceptions with status='scheduled' (extras + reschedule-tos) that land on this week
    const courseIds = new Set(courses.value.map(c => c.id));
    for (let dow = 1; dow <= 7; dow++) {
      const targetDate = getDisplayDateFull(dow);
      const dayExceptions = exceptions.value.filter(ex => 
        ex.schedule_date === targetDate && 
        ex.status === 'scheduled' &&
        (ex.student_course_id == null || courseIds.has(Number(ex.student_course_id)))
      );
      dayExceptions.forEach(ex => {
        if (!filterTeacherId.value || ex.teacher_id === filterTeacherId.value) {
          mergedList.push({
            id: 'ex_' + ex.id,
            original_id: ex.id,
            is_exception: true,
            ...  // maps all fields from the exception row
          });
        }
      });
    }
    return mergedList;
  }

  return list;
});
```

Pipeline summary:
1. `displayWeekFilteredCourses` pre-filters by `weeks` array if a specific week number is selected.
2. Teacher filter applied if `filterTeacherId` is set.
3. In `week` mode, two passes: **suppress** base courses blocked by leave/reschedule exceptions; **inject** `scheduled` exceptions (extras + reschedule targets) as synthetic course objects with `is_exception: true`.

---

## 7. Key Refs

```542:554:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const viewMode = ref('week');
const displayWeek = ref(0);
const weekOffset = ref(0); // 上週/下週偏移
const courses = ref([]);
const exceptions = ref([]); // Store schedules (leaves, extras, reschedules)
const allStudents = ref([]);
const teachers = ref([]);
const filterTeacherId = ref('');
const showModal = ref(false);
const editingCourseId = ref(null);
/** 點擊的那一堂的實際日期（僅編輯單堂時有值），用於限定只能做請假/調課/加課 */
const editingActionDate = ref('');
const conflictWarning = ref('');
```

```464:467:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const now = new Date();
const displayYear = ref(now.getFullYear());
const displayMonth = ref(now.getMonth() + 1); // 1-12
```

- `displayWeek` — 0 means "all weeks"; 1–5 means a specific week of the month.
- `weekOffset` — integer offset applied on top of `displayWeek` for prev/next week navigation.
- `courses` — array of base course records from the `student-classes` API/table.
- `exceptions` — array of `schedules` rows (leaves, extras, reschedule originals and targets).

